On Friday 10 August 2007 00:02, Nathaniel Krause wrote:
> Can someone clarify Lojban's semantic philosophy in this regard? I was
> under the impression that for something to be a ro'erbroda it must by
> definition be an instance of a brode broda and, more broadly, an instance
> of a broda. Is the statement {lo'e ro'erbroda na broda} logically
> contradictory?

I don't know about the philosophy, but lo xajyfi'e cu xarju nagi'enai finpe, 
and {xajyfi'e} occurs in Alice. Some others are {mantycinfo} (an insect, 
unrelated to ants) and {xinfigre} (a cactus fruit, rindo jenai xindo; I 
recently made up this word and this is the first time I've said it). The last 
two also translate their scientific names.

Pierre


